{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic","id":917024,"title":"[2E Hack] Alternative Time Travel magic","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-18T16:16:25-07:00","id":917024,"title":"[2E Hack] Alternative Time Travel magic","content":"After today game session, my players group found corebook written version of <i>\u2018Shifting Sands\u2019</i> spell to be overpowered. From our reading and gameplay it comes to conclusion that Acanthus on Time 3 can easily just rewrite all last 3 turns over and over, until end of time. So here is my own proposed version that makes Disciples and Adepts of Time a bit sweat and will lead to new Paradox dice pools.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Sands (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Special<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage may step back through time a short distance, undoing a few precious seconds. This spell sends the subject back through time a one turn. The subject retains any injuries and Conditions gained in the undone turns, and spent Mana and Willpower do not return. Spells cast on her person in the undone time remain as long as she cast them. All other spells she may have cast or had cast on her in the intervening time are canceled. Until the subject catches up to the present, the distortion caused by this spell is visible under Active Time Mage Sight. Once she does so, any changes she made to history become Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The subject travels back a one more turn. This Reach effect may be applied multiple times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-19-2016, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:22:30-07:00","id":917028,"title":"","content":"This causes the spell to do absolutely nothing without Reach, which seems a step too far given that the worst comparable deficit in other spells is the need to dedicate extra or Advanced spell factors in order for the effect to have a practical outcome (e.g. many spells that one might want Advanced Duration on).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:31:42-07:00","id":917030,"title":"","content":"In combat situation 3-4 turns on Time from Primary Factor<b> is <i>too</i> </b><b>practical outcome</b> - it basically reset whole fight. ( <i>Literally</i> get this on today's game session. ) One turn can save your life - two will can change face of battle. Three or four will resolve combat to non-existing.<br /> <br /> Aiming for running jumping back time to one or two turns is practical solution. Aiming with rules on more just destroy's combat scenes with Acanthus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-18-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T16:45:03-07:00","id":917038,"title":"","content":"This is a problem with the Potency system in general, not Shifting Sands specifically. If you wanna nerf it, just remove the Potency affecting the amount of turns you go back and make it a default one turn, for a Reach make it Potency turns, and for two Reaches make it a scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2535-arthexis","name":"arthexis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2535_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T17:05:30-07:00","id":917046,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917038#post917038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a problem with the Potency system in general, not Shifting Sands specifically.</div> </div> </div> </div>On general I like autmatic 'Arcana dots in Potency' with most of spells. Just in this particular instance this 3-4 is just way too much, on logistical takes of narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>arthexis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917038#post917038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you wanna nerf it, just remove the Potency affecting the amount of turns you go back and make it a default one turn, for a Reach make it Potency turns, and for two Reaches make it a scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>For jumping back on scene or more is <i>Corridors of Time</i> for Masters, not Time 3 spell. Even then, as I mentioned above, 3-4 turns in combat situation means almost sure not live or die combat situation - it's basically 'win button'. I'm okay with this kind things on Masters level - but on Disciples it's just a way too much.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with character risking Paradox to get more than 1-2 turns, rising exponential Dox dice pools. You want to jump more than those 3-6 seconds? Ask your friendly Time Master. If not - just roll with big Paradox... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T17:58:36-07:00","id":917064,"title":"","content":"Shifting Sands was complained about elsewhere, and I made the following suggestion for backwards time traveling spells, specifically for Sands abuse.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How about using a Sound of Thunder/Time and Punishment/Looper model? Rather than playing out the scene or fight again, the caster identifies the outcome he wanted, and the ST imposes a penalty as the cost. Some ideas:<ul><li>The subject may trade any of the following for another option on the list:<ul><li>Damage equal to the spell's Potency (limited by the amount of damage taken in that scene)</li> <li>Gain or lose a Condition</li> <li>Close or open a Door</li> <li>Improve or worsen an Impression, using 1 Reach to flip to or from Hostile</li> <li>Improve or worsen a roll by one step (failure to a success, success to exceptional success), at a cost of 1 Reach if the roll would require a dice trick to achieve</li> <li>Add dice equal to the spell's Potency to rolls leveraging information gained since the target event</li> <li>Describe a plausible difference in events and extrapolate the outcome.</li> </ul></li> <li>The ST then imposes a penalty. She may choose an option above, or another from the list below, or make something up. If she chooses the last option above, she shouldn't cancel or significantly contradict the outcome, but can certainly modify it.<ul><li>The next spell the subject casts gains two Paradox dice.</li> <li>The next successful Paradox roll made against the caster becomes an exceptional success.</li> <li>Impose a Condition.</li> </ul></li> </ul><br /> The idea is to keep the spotlight on the present, impose a cost for altering the past too much, and keep the story moving forward. </div> </div> </div>It's a rough take, and I'd toy with the damage options, but it might be useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T18:21:22-07:00","id":917074,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"969\" data-vbnamecard=\"969\">Verge</a>: That has some promise. My group's Time mage has been reluctant to use Shifting Sands because of the &quot;welp, there goes everything we've done with the last three hours of this session out the save-and-reload window&quot; factor. I think I'll run something like this by him and see if he bites.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-18T20:20:29-07:00","id":917127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917030#post917030\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In combat situation 3-4 turns on Time from Primary Factor<b> is <i>too</i> </b><b>practical outcome</b> - it basically reset whole fight. ( <i>Literally</i> get this on today's game session. ) One turn can save your life - two will can change face of battle. Three or four will resolve combat to non-existing.<br /> <br /> Aiming for running jumping back time to one or two turns is practical solution. Aiming with rules on more just destroy's combat scenes with Acanthus.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it's okay to do at Mastery then it's okay to do earlier in the game. Saying that it's too good or too practical isn't qualitatively useful. You also seem to be forgetting that if the players can do it then so can the NPCs. A time jumping battle is just as likely to eventually have a victor as a more linear one. If you didn't plan on providing an opponent that can skip through time when you know the players can do it then that's not the player's fault and it's not &quot;too practical&quot; it's you making a goof and then complaining about it instead of learning a valuable lesson in STing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T00:22:48-07:00","id":917222,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"969\" data-vbnamecard=\"969\">Verge</a> - it's interesting idea but I think it's sightly unplayable in real game situation. Like, on last game session the Shifting Sands were taken out when other PC changed whole air in one hose into mustard gas to kill rest of them ( it was PVP scenario, Diamond vs Seers ). <i>How</i> to count this as penalty to fight with magic? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's okay to do at Mastery then it's okay to do earlier in the game. Saying that it's too good or too practical isn't qualitatively useful. You also seem to be forgetting that if the players can do it then so can the NPCs. A time jumping battle is just as likely to eventually have a victor as a more linear one. If you didn't plan on providing an opponent that can skip through time when you know the players can do it then that's not the player's fault and it's not &quot;too practical&quot; it's you making a goof and then complaining about it instead of learning a valuable lesson in STing.</div> </div> </div> </div>If what you would say was true spells like Ex Nihilo or Contagion would be on lower dots of Arcanum - but they are not, as they give to much leeway in players hands with this. They are tiers of play in <b>Mage</b> and literally whole mechanic is based on idea that Disciples is a bit different game than Masters.<br /> <br /> So stop thread crapping and if you still think you have right, move along, as this clearly is not topic for you. Let ourselves to hammer new mechanics for time travel in peace.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-19-2016, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T05:34:55-07:00","id":917298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it's okay to do at Mastery then it's okay to do earlier in the game. Saying that it's too good or too practical isn't qualitatively useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>By that same logic, a neonate vampire should have level 5 disciplines. If it ok at &quot;Elder&quot; its okay at &quot;neonate&quot;<br /> <br /> If its okay to have 9-10 primal urge/blood potency at elder then its okay to start a neonate/freshly change werewolf/vampire with primal urge/potency 10.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> You also seem to be forgetting that if the players can do it then so can the NPCs. A time jumping battle is just as likely to eventually have a victor as a more linear one. If you didn't plan on providing an opponent that can skip through time when you know the players can do it then that's not the player's fault and it's not &quot;too practical&quot; it's you making a goof and then complaining about it instead of learning a valuable lesson in STing.</div> </div> </div> </div>so you say that for a combat to have any kind of meaning it has always to have a mage with time which is a contrive at best.<br /> <br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\">wyrdhamster</a></b> I like the rule. Anything to bait PC to use reach <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T07:13:14-07:00","id":917329,"title":"","content":"You're missing my point, which is that if you don't like a character having the power to travel through time at 3 dots, you're not going to like it any better at 5. It's not the level that the power comes in at that is being discussed as the problem here, it's the power itself.<br /> <br /> I'm also not saying that you are required to have a Mage with time to make combat meaningful. I'm saying that you need to take time travel into account when you plan out your encounters.<br /> <br /> I'm not trying to thread crap, I'm trying to help point out that your real problem here is that you are being challenged by an unfamiliar situation and your reflexive resistance to it is not helping you create a better game by growing as an ST to handle a broader range of possible actions that your players can take. Basically, this rule change exists simply to be convenient to you instead of to contribute to making the game better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:04:18-07:00","id":917379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917329#post917329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing my point, which is that if you don't like a character having the power to travel through time at 3 dots, you're not going to like it any better at 5. It's not the level that the power comes in at that is being discussed as the problem here, it's the power itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's you who miss the point - I do not have problem with power on Master level ( well, I think about limiting it's more to rather scenes, but it's not the point ). Disciples powers are totally different than Masters ones - And <i>Shifting Sands</i> let you use what was spoilered before premiere as Master power ( literary I remember reading from <b>DaveB</b> that Time 3 let you to move back in turns times and only Time 5 to make return in scenes) - and that's a point.<br /> <br /> I got noting wrong to let Time mages jumps back in time. I<b> have</b> with idea <i>how far</i> they can go this to not irritate other co-players.<br /> <br /> They are power levels built in Arcana and <i>Shifting Sands</i> seems, RAW, as coming from Master level when he makes too easy to just win any confrontation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917329#post917329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not saying that you are required to have a Mage with time to make combat meaningful. I'm saying that you need to take time travel into account when you plan out your encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Making Acanthus rewrite time for non cost ( RAW spell do not even cost Mana! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ) means that anyone would need to kill all opposite Acanthi first, to make sure they do not change time. And whole combat just change in to 'shoot Acanthus first' contest. Not cool, play-wise, I say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917329#post917329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to thread crap, I'm trying to help point out that your real problem here is that you are being challenged by an unfamiliar situation and your reflexive resistance to it is not helping you create a better game by growing as an ST to handle a broader range of possible actions that your players can take. Basically, this rule change exists simply to be convenient to you instead of to contribute to making the game better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if all my gaming group AND me as ST see this power as totally overpower - I call it just bad written power. We had on yesterday game night literal tornado everyone do not gritt they teeth on that, only thinking it's cool power. But when Time mage use <i>Shifting Sands</i> easily and we understood that it him cost nothing to repeat that in the same scene - it's really broken.<br /> <br /> \u200bMister <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a>, after this and other previous posts to my on last few days - I start to think you are trolling me, so I will not answer on more your posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-19-2016, 02:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:08:45-07:00","id":917380,"title":"","content":"A spell that does literally nothing unless you Reach is a poorly designed spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T09:28:43-07:00","id":917392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917380#post917380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A spell that does literally nothing unless you Reach is a poorly designed spell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking on it - you have right, I should give option to jump one turn on basis of it. Edited first post and alternative spell description. Thanks for pointing it out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:09:31-07:00","id":917516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917379#post917379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's you who miss the point - I do not have problem with power on Master level ( well, I think about limiting it's more to rather scenes, but it's not the point ). Disciples powers are totally different than Masters ones - And <i>Shifting Sands</i> let you use what was spoilered before premiere as Master power ( literary I remember reading from <b>DaveB</b> that Time 3 let you to move back in turns times and only Time 5 to make return in scenes) - and that's a point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand why you think it's okay at Mastery but not earlier. My point is that you're just kicking the can down the road, when your player's become Masters you'll be right back to this same problem of time travel being a hassle and over powered. <br /> <br /> If your entire group has decided they don't want to deal with the challenges that can be presented by time travel then that's fine. It doesn't mean the power is badly designed though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T13:47:19-07:00","id":917541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917298#post917298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\">wyrdhamster</a></b> I like the rule. Anything to bait PC to use reach <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I just understood that Reach option means that with Rote you are more or less safe from it's consequences with Masters Reaches - well, at least you need Rote for it to work easier, like it's in now on straight RAW. And no resetting on scenes, till proper Master of Time on PCs and it's <i>Corridors of Time</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T14:22:04-07:00","id":917550,"title":"","content":"You could use half the Potency for the time traveled (so 4 Potency becomes 2 turns, 6 Potency becomes 3 turns, and so on).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T14:23:55-07:00","id":917552,"title":"","content":"I have not read the second edition yet but that magic left me really worried. I've had huge problems in adapting the first edition time spells. I was not expecting to see more problems in 2e. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I hope the rest of the game is much more consistent, with fewer gray areas as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T14:27:14-07:00","id":917555,"title":"","content":"You could play the game without published spells, using just Creative Thaumaturgy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T14:38:16-07:00","id":917560,"title":"","content":"Thinking more on Rote problem with Reach take on spell variant, I come to conclusion to give basic spell 1 turn jump and for only available +2 Reach you can move one turn more - on improvised casting it quickly lead to Paradox rolls. On Rote you can easily jump 3 turns ( 1 basic + 2 turns from Reach 4 options ), which is kinda okay for Rote version, I think. Higher cost Reach will be too much to cast it. I've edited first post with it.<br /> <br /> If any one have other ideas how to bite the topic - just post it. I'm still can see other ideas on fixing <i>Shifting Sands</i> spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:16:05-07:00","id":917573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917392#post917392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looking on it - you have right</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel a bit snubbed given that this was in fact the very first thing I pointed out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:20:20-07:00","id":917575,"title":"","content":"There-there <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar111_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"111\" data-vbnamecard=\"111\">Satchel</a> - you were right. Here, happy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:29:36-07:00","id":917578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Shifting Sands (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Special<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage may step back through time a short distance, undoing a few precious seconds. This spell sends the subject back through time a number of turns in Reach used on it. The subject retains any injuries and Conditions gained in the undone turns, and spent Mana and Willpower do not return. Spells cast on her person in the undone time remain as long as she cast them. All other spells she may have cast or had cast on her in the intervening time are canceled. Until the subject catches up to the present, the distortion caused by this spell is visible under Active Time Mage Sight. Once she does so, any changes she made to history become Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject travels back a one turn. This Reach effect may be applied multiple times. </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's a typo, but you should get at least one turn of time travel from the spell, and the spell should have an actual primary spell factor, even if it's a neutered Potency for dispellation purposes. Also, the spell doesn't have any utility as an extended casting, so the free Reach is essentially wasted. Half of the options of an Exceptional Success are gone with a &quot;special&quot; primary factor, making it less valuable as a Praxis, and diminishing the power of Yantras in its casting.<br /> <br /> Suggestions: first, back to Potency. Next, get one 'free turn' of time travel. OR, the subject can revise the turn's action with a bonus equal to Potency, or change the target of the action, or choose a different action, or apply a modifier to another character's dice pool for that turn or the present turn. +1 Reach extends the depth of the time travel by another turn's worth (multiple applications). +1 Reach applies a dice trick to rolls affected by the spell. Find some way to make it useful in extended castings, or at least some way where it's useful outside combat situations. I'd feel pretty cheated were I an Acanthus player getting nerfed on <i>the </i>spell that exemplifies Time magic's power.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":".  Edit: Whoops, changes already getting made. 06-19-2016, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:43:35-07:00","id":917587,"title":"","content":"Forum engine makes some pranks and I cannot edit Opening Post of topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Here is now version of my fixed <i>Shifting Sands </i>on 'Reach version'.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Sands (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Special<br /> <b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage may step back through time a short distance, undoing a few precious seconds. This spell sends the subject back through time a one turn. The subject retains any injuries and Conditions gained in the undone turns, and spent Mana and Willpower do not return. Spells cast on her person in the undone time remain as long as she cast them. All other spells she may have cast or had cast on her in the intervening time are canceled. Until the subject catches up to the present, the distortion caused by this spell is visible under Active Time Mage Sight. Once she does so, any changes she made to history become Lasting.<br /> <br /> <b>+2 Reach:</b> The subject travels back a one more turn. This Reach effect may be applied multiple times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T15:59:50-07:00","id":917596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917578#post917578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's a typo, but you should get at least one turn of time travel from the spell,</div> </div> </div> </div>It's in now version of Reach variant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917578#post917578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the spell should have an actual primary spell factor, even if it's a neutered Potency for dispellation purposes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, you are right - if Potency do not do anything to the spell effects itself, it can be easily Primary Factor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917578#post917578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the spell doesn't have any utility as an extended casting, so the free Reach is essentially wasted. Half of the options of an Exceptional Success are gone with a &quot;special&quot; primary factor, making it less valuable as a Praxis, and diminishing the power of Yantras in its casting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't like it, don't use it - <i>whole concept</i> for it that it should not be more tweaked about by mages. Only Reach should change in it.<br /> <br /> But I still have question HOW &quot;Special&quot; Primary Factor destroys Exceptional Success?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917578#post917578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'd feel pretty cheated were I an Acanthus player getting nerfed on <i>the </i>spell that exemplifies Time magic's power.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't like it, don't use it - corebook version is still in book. Even our Acanthus player said books version is broken, so we changing this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T16:37:31-07:00","id":917618,"title":"","content":"Potency doesn't have anything to do with Dispellation. Dispellation doesn't interact with Potency. Dispellation interacts with Arcana rating of the spellcaster; if you have Time 3, your spell will have Withstand 3 against Dispellation, even if it has 900000000000000 Potency banked in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T17:06:31-07:00","id":917639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917596#post917596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't like it, don't use it - corebook version is still in book. Even our Acanthus player said books version is broken, so we changing this one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Never assumed I could change your mind. I don't necessarily agree that it's overpowered, but I will concede that it's disruptive to play turns and scenes again. If I get a little pushy, it's about trying to provoke a creative solution, rather than judgment. (tl;dr, it's friendly creative resistance).<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917596#post917596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I still have question HOW &quot;Special&quot; Primary Factor destroys Exceptional Success?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't destroy it, it just diminishes it. You can take an extra Reach or point in the Primary Spell Factor on an exceptional success, or you can ignore Withstand loss. That leaves two other options to the Shifter of Sands: an Arcane Beat Condition, or a full Mana Refund + 1WP. Special isn't defined, nor is it consistent with other spell factors, which takes it out of established spellcasting rules, and consequently economy. A G1 Acanthus can't mitigate Paradox in the same turn he attempts this spell, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":969,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","user":"Verge","date":". 06-19-2016, 08:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T20:31:21-07:00","id":917752,"title":"","content":"<br /> Oh i know im not suppose to feed the trolls but.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not trying to thread crap, I'm trying to help point out that your real problem here is that you are being challenged by an unfamiliar situation and your reflexive resistance to it is not helping you create a better game by growing as an ST to handle a broader range of possible actions that your players can take.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually you kinda are<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it's you making a goof and then complaining about it instead of learning a valuable lesson in STing.</div> </div> </div> </div>This comment in incredibly condescending, specially when you cant put your money where your mouth is because<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917329#post917329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also not saying that you are required to have a Mage with time to make combat meaningful. I'm saying that you need to take time travel into account when you plan out your encounters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually your only contribution was<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also seem to be forgetting that if the players can do it then so can the NPCs. A time jumping battle is just as likely to eventually have a victor as a more linear one. If you didn't plan on <u><b>providing an opponent that can skip</b> through time</u> when you know the players can do it then that's not the player's fault and it's not &quot;too practical&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly that, or barring a mage some kind of time travelling entity which is kinda the same thing.<br /> <br /> So you say that houserulling to remove a problematic element by table consensus is<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917127#post917127\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, this rule change exists simply to be convenient to you instead of to contribute to making the game better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that you a fan and think the game is 100% perfect and anyone who disagrees just &quot;doesnt get it&quot; but posting in threads of people with actual problems with the game and saying &quot;you just dont get it, you should get better at ST&quot; without contributing any useful solution is threadcrapping.<br /> <br /> So tell us, how would you fix Wyrdhamster problem without.....either enemy Time mage, Counterspell (which is the same as removing it) or Narrative contrivance (butterfly effect).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917516#post917516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't understand why you think it's okay at Mastery but not earlier. My point is that you're just kicking the can down the road, when your player's become Masters you'll be right back to this same problem of time travel being a hassle and over powered.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because its a different power level entirely, mage of all games have a huge gap between different levels of arcana and the game play slightly different with a entire party of arcanum 2 to 3 and 3 to 4 and so on.<br /> <br /> Also depends on the table and what power level the game is gonna reach player wise. I read A LOT of people in this forum before 2ed that consider master and archmastery to just another level like getting 4 in a attribute but not all tables/players use the same measuring sticks. I cant talk about Wyrdhamster table but in mine that an spell/attaiment is arcanum 2 or 5 is a huge difference.<br /> <br /> Why? Because 2 means im gonna have to deal with it from day 0. And that every player could get it easily. I also have to assume that this exploit is present in the setting (which the setting as written practically ignores) and how that affect npcs.<br /> <br /> 5 on the other hands means that only a small subsection of NPCs (maybe 2 or 3) is gonna have it. On the player front when they reach mastery the game is ending and honestly when you have a table of master mages, then one has an entirely different game. If a master of time can make most direct combat meaningless, its okay because whats left of the game? 3 or 4 sessions? In which most storylines are wrapping so maybe 2 or 3 big combats at most? And thats face to face, in PBP mastery is not for players, its epilogue stuff or maybe just maybe 1 player who plays the whole 3 years.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 06-19-2016, 11:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T20:31:57-07:00","id":917753,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917587#post917587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forum engine makes some pranks and I cannot edit Opening Post of topic. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=917587#post917587\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Here is now version of my fixed <i>Shifting Sands </i>on 'Reach version'.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Shifting Sands (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Practice:</b> Fraying</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Primary Factor:</b> Special</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Cost:</b> 1 Mana</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The mage may step back through time a short distance, undoing a few precious seconds. This spell sends the subject back through time a one turn. The subject retains any injuries and Conditions gained in the undone turns, and spent Mana and Willpower do not return. Spells cast on her person in the undone time remain as long as she cast them. All other spells she may have cast or had cast on her in the intervening time are canceled. Until the subject catches up to the present, the distortion caused by this spell is visible under Active Time Mage Sight. Once she does so, any changes she made to history become Lasting.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>+2 Reach:</b> The subject travels back a one more turn. This Reach effect may be applied multiple times.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">As verge suggested there is no exceptional result to make it worthy as a praxys. What about with exceptiona success PC doesnt retains injury, as it is a combat-only spell, PCs are never gonna be able to cast this in optimal conditions</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T20:46:20-07:00","id":917756,"title":"","content":"Actually, I don't think the game is perfect, but if talking about differences at the table is something you want to do...well okay. I have a group that's working its way through Reign of the Exarchs that's running on 1.5 rules, they aren't halfway through and yet all of them are at least 1st degree Masters by now. Time shennanigans have been a feature for a while now. Are the range of options available to the players broader? Yeah, of course it is, but when you are able to take those things into account you can create a game that isn't going to hit as many hiccups just because someone can jump through time.<br /> <br /> If removing or heavily restricting time travel is what Wyrd needs to do to make the game work for him, that's fine. It still isn't an actual indication that the mechanic itself is broken or bad. My useful solution isn't aimed at mechanics, it's true, but if you think that any given ST doesn't have room to improve his ability to run a game then you're gravely mistaken. I'm not saying that Wyrd (Or any ST who has problems with time travel) is a bad ST, I'm raising the question of is he trying to learn from this experience that made him uncomfortable or is he reflexively moving to what he's been comfortable with in the past rather than trying to improve?<br /> <br /> In other words, my useful solution is to think critically, is it the game mechanic or is it the ST that needs to change? Since there have been a number of threads on time travel and how to handle it already I'd suggest going to look at those. Charlaquin and Arthexis have both had some pretty insightful things to say about it.<br /> <br /> By the way your assumption that the game's mechanics don't match the fluff is flawed. We don't know the complete story of the characters involved. The Present in Mage is set as a continuously moving point and the future is in flux. The Past is set until events in the Present change it. The events in the story were set in the (or a recent) Present. If we continued to follow the characters we might find that the main character did in fact learn Time eventually and manage to succeed in preventing the death of her partner. It doesn't necessarily service the piece of fiction to take into account all points in the timeline of what comes next, and since the story is set so closely to the Present and the future is in flux it cannot in fact be known yet if the Past will change. This can in fact be directly mimicked by the way the actual game is played. You don't play the game as if the future has already happened, you play as if you're experiencing the Present when you don't have the skill with Time to change the Past. Maybe later in the chronicle your character will feel driven by guilt to learn Time in order to go back and rectify her mistakes, but -right now- you can't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-19-2016, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-19T21:58:18-07:00","id":917795,"title":"","content":"As to Exceptional Success on 'Reach variant' - One Free Reach is kinda good for spell as it lowers yours Paradox dicepool. Idea about not sustaining wounds is really interesting, I need to think about it.<br /> <br /> As to Primary Factor: Special - it's taken exactly so to omit normal rules 'you get Arcanum dots in Primary Factor'. If Gnosis 1 mages only have problem with this and need to spend two turns on it casting - I do not have qualms with it. Mana cost of spell was introduced to lower 'spell spamming' - when you need to spend 1 Mana on spell AND 1-3 to Paradox mitigation, you will consider your options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T10:58:12-07:00","id":918127,"title":"","content":"So, in the interest of throwing out ideas for how to handle time travel problems narratively when you don't have a time traveling antagonist:<br /> <br /> Make it difficult to use time travel in the place where the bad guys are located. Maybe they're holed up in a place like an Ansho. <br /> <br /> Have plot critical scenes happen at time sensitive junctures. In other words the PCs show up right as the bad guy is about to complete their evil plan. This way if a PC goes back, any time he spends trying to be better prepared is time not spent toward getting to that critical point when the bad guy is just about to succeed.<br /> <br /> Have multiple things happen at once or in close proximity. If the PC jumps back in order to prepare better or get to the critical event sooner then he runs the risk of not achieving some goal that happened very recently such as having an important interview with the Heirarch. You can also effectively use splitting the party to achieve a similar effect, the PC can't go back to tell his buddy to be better buffed because the buddy is having the important Heirarch interview.<br /> <br /> A scene is roughly a half-hour to an hour, but it's not chronologically precise. Within the framework of how many scenes a PC goes back via his Reach you can plop him down just about anywhere making for some possibly tense, awkward or plot fueling consequences.<br /> <br /> The bad guys can move while the PCs delay to be better prepared. Maybe they're done with their hidey-hole or step out for coffee.<br /> <br /> If you do end up needing to replay a scene you can speed it up by reusing the results of dice rolls unless someone performs a different action from what they did last time. Only the time traveller really knows what is or isn't different (This one could require some good cooperative roleplaying and a bit of metagaming) and so can communicate what needs to change. Restrict his ability to do this communication (I.e. No blabbing out a whole plan of a different course of action as a free action).<br /> <br /> I think using strategies like this and devising more of them would do a lot to improve the ability of an ST to run a game without attempting to rewrite the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T11:32:01-07:00","id":918151,"title":"","content":"I've pitched all my objections to the revised spell. Hope it works for your group, Wyrd!<br /> <br /> So, this has me thinking about &quot;temporal Cold War&quot; solutions to time travel. My number one goal with Time magic is to fold it in to the narrative, rather than iterate over a moment again. Has anyone given thought to adapting the Anticipation rules in <b>Mirrors</b> to the problem? I always skipped over the chapter, as it was a little too &quot;little did you know&quot; for my liking, but what I remember of it seems like it could be implemented here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T03:15:24-07:00","id":918524,"title":"","content":"So topic died for now? I have a question if someone also thinks that <i>Corridors of Time</i> are a bit too much, even for Time 5 level? I'm not sure if easy jumping in your own timeline can be solved in time of game narrative to not collide with other players expectations at table...<br /> <br /> My alternative would be to stick to Potency in hours for it - just I'm not sure is it really needed. It's more of the question if <b>Butterfly Effect</b> can be done without upsetting other players - or we should just stick to <b>Run, Lola, Run</b> kind of variant.<br /> <br /> <b>Run, Lola, Run</b> works like this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=e83ZEb3jYv8\" data-code=\"e83ZEb3jYv8\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/e83ZEb3jYv8/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> <b>Butterfly Effect</b> works like this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=B8_dgqfPXFg\" data-code=\"B8_dgqfPXFg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/B8_dgqfPXFg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T05:38:36-07:00","id":918572,"title":"","content":"A lot of these problems sound more like player expectation problems than Time problems. You're blanketly gutting the things Time is supposed to be capable of to avoid clashing with player expectations. I'm assuming you've actually talked to the players involved and they all agree this is necessary in your game?<br /> <br /> Running a game with an Acanthus is a very specific type of game. If your players aren't up for that, it might be worth just not having an Acanthus instead of beating their power-level into the ground.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:19:23-07:00","id":918586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=918572#post918572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of these problems sound more like player expectation problems than Time problems. You're blanketly gutting the things Time is supposed to be capable of to avoid clashing with player expectations. I'm assuming you've actually talked to the players involved and they all agree this is necessary in your game?</div> </div> </div> </div>We spend about 30 minutes of our game time on how <i>Shifting Sands</i> are now overpowered. Everyone agreed it's too much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=918572#post918572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Running a game with an Acanthus is a very specific type of game. If your players aren't up for that, it might be worth just not having an Acanthus instead of beating their power-level into the ground.</div> </div> </div> </div>We are literally 50 session after start of campaign - we run two years before on 1.5E version of rules. And we did not have any problems with Acanthus players ( or any Time users ) on previous spells as they were limited in scope. I was looking for 2E on spoilered Time spells that worked in matters of turns and hours, not near-Archmastery 'I change my entire life and everything with you in it' that is in corebook.<br /> <br /> Solution of 'not using Acanthus in game' is <i>not solution for me</i> - I love Acanthus! I'm myself Acanthus at heart. Just 2E corebook Time Travel magic is so much overpowered compared to 1E it makes Acanthus players unplayable in the same group with other Paths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-21-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:37:50-07:00","id":918597,"title":"","content":"&quot;The game works fine if you just don't play it&quot; isn't saying good things about it :P.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T06:43:18-07:00","id":918600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=918586#post918586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spend about 30 minutes in-game time on how <i>Shifting Sands</i> are now overpowered. Everyone agreed it's too much.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> We are literally 50 session after start of campaign - we run two years before on 1.5E version of rules. And we did not have any problems with Acanthus players ( or any Time users ) on previews spells as they were limited in scope. I was looking for 2E on spoilered Time spells that worked in matters of turns and hours, not near-Archmastery 'I change my entire life and everything with you in it' that is in corebook.<br /> <br /> Solution of 'not using Acanthus in game' is <i>not solution for me</i> - I love Acanthus! I'm myself Acanthus at heart. Just 2E corebook Time Travel magic is so much overpowered compared to 1E it makes Acanthus players unplayable in the same group with other Paths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been following the topic and clearly understand what you mean.<br /> Time spells tend to greatly harm the narrative or immensely confuse the combat.<br /> It is not a matter of not using Acanthus as they say there, it is frustrating when the rules do not give a clear ground on the limitations.<br /> I spent the weekend to read Mage 2e and my god, I do not know if I have the courage to start a game yet. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">With a bit of magic everything can be done.</span></span><br /> <b>All WoD gamelines wallpapers <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...all-nwod-games\" target=\"_blank\">here! </a></b></i></span></span><br /> <i><b>Choose your favorite or create your own!</b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/866-magisanctum","name":"magisanctum","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar866_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T07:00:59-07:00","id":918604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=918597#post918597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The game works fine if you just don't play it&quot; isn't saying good things about it :P.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty disingenuous representation of what I said.<br /> <br /> The scope of what Acanthus can do requires a lot of buy-in and certain expectations from your players. If your players have neither, you can either gut their abilities or not use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:19:16-07:00","id":918632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>magisanctum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=918600#post918600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have been following the topic and clearly understand what you mean.<br /> Time spells tend to greatly harm the narrative or immensely confuse the combat.<br /> It is not a matter of not using Acanthus as they say there, it is frustrating when the rules do not give a clear ground on the limitations.<br /> I spent the weekend to read Mage 2e and my god, I do not know if I have the courage to start a game yet. </div> </div> </div> </div>What narrative? The STs? The players are there to contribute to the narrative that is being created by the group. Being able to change time isn't harmful to the narrative, it's simply part of it. I'll grant, it can be a challenging part of it, but we shouldn't let that stop us from tackling it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T05:46:29-07:00","id":919050,"title":"","content":"remove this","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-22-2016, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T05:46:29-07:00","id":919051,"title":"","content":"for some reason, timelines started converging and my post posted multiple times. oops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T06:06:09-07:00","id":919057,"title":"","content":"...ok, im really annoyed with the forum software, as it first replicated my post 4 times, and now it ate the only I left unedited with my original post.<br /> <br /> Anyway, because I don't have all day:<br /> <br /> 1. Add 1 Mana cost to the Shifting Sands.<br /> 2. Add following line to the spell itself: &quot;Character casting or targeted by this spell gains Temporally Unstable Condition. Resolving it does not grant Beats.&quot;<br /> 3.<br /> TEMPORALLY UNSTABLE<br /> You are currently wrestling with Sands of Time, trying to manipulate the past. This makes any further attempts at Time Travel harder and more complicated; any attempts at Time Travelling demand 1 Mana in addition to any other costs, in order to lubricate the Timestream. This cost grows by 1 for each Time Travel attempted during this Condition's duration. This cost also isn't a part of the spell itself, so effects that allow to bypass it - like Attainment's Mana Refund, or Exceptional Success at Spellcasting - don't interact with it. You may not spend multiple turns to pay this special cost, you need to pay it in one go.<br /> Possible Sources: Shifting Sands spell, using a Time Machine<br /> Resolution: Start of a new scene that wasn't initiated by Time Travel.<br /> Hardcore Version Resolution: End of the original scene that was Time Travelled from, or of the scene that will take it's place in new timeline.<br /> <br /> What it does:<br /> It doesn't limit how far you can time travel, but it limits the spamming problem. It basically puts a cap of how many times you can use Shifting Sands in a scene equal to your Gnosis, *and* it drains your Mana like crazy. This introduces a common trope in Time Travel Stories, where characters have a limited number of &quot;repeats&quot;, and can't just replay at their leisure until they win, as they have to make the most from their spare time. The Hardcore Version could be used when characters are traveling SCENES, not TURNS, so you have only, let's say, 2 chances to save your friend from being terribly murdered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 06-22-2016, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T06:38:55-07:00","id":919067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=919057#post919057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...ok, im really annoyed with the forum software, as it first replicated my post 4 times, and now it ate the only I left unedited with my original post.<br /> <br /> Anyway, because I don't have all day:<br /> <br /> 1. Add 1 Mana cost to the Shifting Sands.<br /> 2. Add following line to the spell itself: &quot;Character casting or targeted by this spell gains Temporally Unstable Condition. Resolving it does not grant Beats.&quot;<br /> 3.<br /> TEMPORALLY UNSTABLE<br /> You are currently wrestling with Sands of Time, trying to manipulate the past. This makes any further attempts at Time Travel harder and more complicated; any attempts at Time Travelling demand 1 Mana in addition to any other costs, in order to lubricate the Timestream. This cost grows by 1 for each Time Travel attempted during this Condition's duration. This cost also isn't a part of the spell itself, so effects that allow to bypass it - like Attainment's Mana Refund, or Exceptional Success at Spellcasting - don't interact with it. You may not spend multiple turns to pay this special cost, you need to pay it in one go.<br /> Possible Sources: Shifting Sands spell, using a Time Machine<br /> Resolution: Start of a new scene that wasn't initiated by Time Travel.<br /> Hardcore Version Resolution: End of the original scene that was Time Travelled from, or of the scene that will take it's place in new timeline.<br /> <br /> What it does:<br /> It doesn't limit how far you can time travel, but it limits the spamming problem. It basically puts a cap of how many times you can use Shifting Sands in a scene equal to your Gnosis, *and* it drains your Mana like crazy. This introduces a common trope in Time Travel Stories, where characters have a limited number of &quot;repeats&quot;, and can't just replay at their leisure until they win, as they have to make the most from their spare time. The Hardcore Version could be used when characters are traveling SCENES, not TURNS, so you have only, let's say, 2 chances to save your friend from being terribly murdered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this a lot, and I don't even take issue with Time as it is currently. This is very thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T09:50:40-07:00","id":919776,"title":"","content":"Wyrd, for your high Gnosis group - try switching growth of the extra cost from flat 1 Mana to the same number as Paradox-Per-Reach-By-Gnosis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:10:51-07:00","id":919786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=919776#post919776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyrd, for your high Gnosis group - try switching growth of the extra cost from flat 1 Mana to the same number as Paradox-Per-Reach-By-Gnosis?</div> </div> </div> </div>Solution that need to be tweaked for each gaming group is bad solution for basis of time traveling spells...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T10:50:47-07:00","id":919810,"title":"","content":"That would be like saying that Paradox scaling with Gnosis is tweaked per-group. In fact, this would keep the number of replays down to 1 or 2 over all gnosis levels, I think *too tired to math it out*.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying, make the growing cost use the same variable as Paradox, instead of it always being 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-23T13:08:04-07:00","id":919889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=919057#post919057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...ok, im really annoyed with the forum software, as it first replicated my post 4 times, and now it ate the only I left unedited with my original post.</div> </div> </div> </div>When this kind of thing happens, feel free to flag the post and include a description of what went wrong. If it's something a mod can fix, this will help us notice it faster, and if it's not, it doesn't hurt anything. We can view previous versions of posts that have been edited, so in this case I could have recovered the original version of your post. Technically I could still do it if you want, but it seems the conversation has moved on and I'm not sure if it would still be relevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T00:01:01-07:00","id":920221,"title":"","content":"Been pondering on Shifting Sands whole afternoon and taking inspirations from <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar9102_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"9102\" data-vbnamecard=\"9102\">WHW</a> I come to this version, based on rising Paradox and extra Codition for it.<br /> <br /> <b>Shifting Sands (Time \u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Practice:</b> Fraying<br /> <b>Primary Factor:</b> Potency<br /> <b>Cost: </b>1 Mana<br /> <b>Suggested Rote Skills:</b> Academics, Occult, Survival<br /> <br /> The mage may step back through time a short distance, undoing a few precious seconds. This spell sends the subject back through time a number of turns in Potency used on it. However, if character step back more than his Time dots, he gain <i>Temporally Unstable</i> Condition. The subject retains any injuries and Conditions gained in the undone turns, and spent Mana and Willpower do not return. Spells cast on her person in the undone time remain as long as she cast them. All other spells she may have cast or had cast on her in the intervening time are cancelled. Until the subject catches up to the present, the distortion caused by this spell is visible under Active Time Mage Sight. Once she does so, any changes she made to history become Lasting. On Exceptional Success with spellcasting, character can have their Health from time to where they step back.<br /> <br /> <b>+1 Reach:</b> The subject travels back a one turn more, up to Potency of spell. However, if number of turns is greater than Time dots of character, she gains <i>Temporally Unstable</i> Condition, with extra Paradox Dice to roll. This Reach effect may be applied multiple times.<br /> <br /> <b>TEMPORALLY UNSTABLE</b><br /> Your character\u2019s Time Pattern had been majorly changed. Temporal instability makes character very dangerous to be subject for Time magic. For duration of one scene (hour), every Time spell cast on her is automatic Paradox inducing. After this period, her Time Pattern stabilize and new temporal magic are safe to use.<br /> <b>Possible Sources:</b> <i>Shifting Sands </i>spell, using a Time Machine<br /> <b>Resolution:</b> Start of a new scene. Waiting one hour.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=919810#post919810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I'm saying, make the growing cost use the same variable as Paradox, instead of it always being 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m much more stick to the Paradox itself \u2013 flat Mana costs makes you only want to sacrifice you more of your Pattern. Rising Paradox danger is much more interesting and can lead to very interesting scenes. It\u2019s also much more \u2018let Mage players hang themselves\u2019. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T03:04:14-07:00","id":920271,"title":"","content":"Temporally Unstable: You should make that all time spells cast on the one with the Condition risk Paradox, not induce Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T02:15:44-08:00","id":1011420,"title":"","content":"After playing whole <b>Life is Strange </b>I start to wonder that maybe letting on Time 5 spell version to jump back to the subjects Representative Sympathy Yantra ( like her picture or paint ), even decades later? It would very high on Reach ( maybe like 5 or even 7 ), but doable by Time Masters. Still, I think about as implications to the game world could be too much - like each Time Master would try to be photographer or painter just to capture as much his own Sympathy Yantra as he can. What do you think about it in contexts of few hours original Time 5 spell?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T07:38:32-08:00","id":1011493,"title":"","content":"Time 5 already allows you to go back decades, or to send something else back decades so I have no idea what you're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:04:24-08:00","id":1011500,"title":"","content":"Protag of Life Is Strange gains ability to target photographs and &quot;jump&quot; into the moment they were took, basically. I think he wants a similar ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T08:23:41-08:00","id":1011508,"title":"","content":"Corridors of Time already allows you to go back decades and requires a Sympathy Yantra if your Temporal Sympathy with the target time is any weaker than Unchanged. It's exactly the spell Wyrd is looking for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T09:54:37-08:00","id":1011543,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, so then my question how to make Corridors of Time work as sometimes story element, but not giving this on every day usage ( like in package of Time Mastery )? Like letting something done this once, maybe twice in chronicle. Just saying that is Mystery and some lucky Acanthi get 'present' of making wrong one, maybe two decisions? The Oracles? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:31:47-08:00","id":1011559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1011543#post1011543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, so then my question how to make Corridors of Time work as sometimes story element, but not giving this on every day usage ( like in package of Time Mastery )? Like letting something done this once, maybe twice in chronicle. Just saying that is Mystery and some lucky Acanthi get 'present' of making wrong one, maybe two decisions? The Oracles? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I am not able to parse your question. Would you mind rephrasing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T10:39:48-08:00","id":1011563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1011559#post1011559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not able to parse your question. Would you mind rephrasing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically he means, &quot;How can I use Corridors of Time for interesting events while still not letting my players use it?&quot; because he hasn't been able to handle time travel in the Mage setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T11:10:49-08:00","id":1011584,"title":"","content":"Oh. You could just give them like an Artifact or something that can cast Corridors of Time but only does so under highly specific conditions, like a particular celestial alignment that happens once every thousand years or whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:07:00-08:00","id":1015902,"title":"","content":"While I haven't run into the same issue at my table (my players aren't bothered by how powerful time travel is) I have still hacked Shifting Sands.<br /> <br /> We realized that if in a Verge or Demesne, paradox can't happen -- and RAW Shifting Sands can travel back as many Reach as you are willing to spend. I couldn't find a limitation on maximum Reach spending, so we had theoretically just used Shifting Sands to go back as far as we liked. That seemed against the intention of Corridors of Time being a Mastery effect.<br /> <br /> The reach option now reads &quot;The mage may jump one scene per Potency, instead of one turn.&quot; and costs 3 reach; effectively making it so jumping Scenes always includes <i>some</i> risk of Paradox, barring huge potency ritual casts from high-Gnosis mages.<br /> <br /> I was a little sad to see the &quot;You can go as far back as you're willing to brave the dox pool&quot; concept go; but ultimately it's the only spell that works like that (that I found, at least).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:24:52-08:00","id":1015907,"title":"","content":"Quick fix is to make it so that both your current position and &quot;temporal destination&quot; of Shifting Sands have to be in the Dox-Free zone in order for it to work. Shifting 10 minutes, which is when you entered the Demesne? No Dox. Shifting 11 minutes, which is just outside of it? Unleash the dox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:36:55-08:00","id":1015909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1015902#post1015902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We realized that if in a Verge or Demesne, paradox can't happen</div> </div> </div> </div>For applicable spells. That's an important detail to remember, given that the semiotic associations of &quot;traveling back in time&quot; are not commonplace.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:39:32-08:00","id":1015910,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1015907#post1015907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick fix is to make it so that both your current position and &quot;temporal destination&quot; of Shifting Sands have to be in the Dox-Free zone in order for it to work. Shifting 10 minutes, which is when you entered the Demesne? No Dox. Shifting 11 minutes, which is just outside of it? Unleash the dox.</div> </div> </div> </div></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We dabbled with the idea that the time traveler couldn't leave the area of the Demesne physically, in the past, but decided against it. Another fix would be to rule that if you traveled outside of the demesne's time of 'creation' it wouldn't apply, either. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I suggested to limit repetitions of the as-worded to the potency of the spell, but ultimately that didn't feel elegant enough a solution and there was no precedent for that in the rest of the published spells. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We also considered \u201cTack a mana onto it!\u201d but that only passed the problem off to tass gathering rather than fixing it. </span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T17:42:59-08:00","id":1015912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1015909#post1015909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For applicable spells. That's an important detail to remember, given that the semiotic associations of &quot;traveling back in time&quot; are not commonplace.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was under the impression that this limitation only applied to the Yantra bonus; not to the paradox limitations. Though, going back and reading it again, your interpretation of those paragraphs seems much more accurate. TY!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Storytelling is the art of pretending you totally meant for that to happen just now.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12721-evilsqueegee","name":"EvilSqueegee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12721_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T00:43:10-08:00","id":1016017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilSqueegee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1015910#post1015910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">We dabbled with the idea that the time traveler couldn't leave the area of the Demesne physically, in the past, but decided against it. Another fix would be to rule that if you traveled outside of the demesne's time of 'creation' it wouldn't apply, either. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I suggested to limit repetitions of the as-worded to the potency of the spell, but ultimately that didn't feel elegant enough a solution and there was no precedent for that in the rest of the published spells. </span></div> </div> </div> </div>You can solve Demesne problem with Temporal Unstable Condition - once your own Pattern is creating Paradox, even Demesne will not save you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-12T01:51:30-08:00","id":1016034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/917024-2e-hack-alternative-time-travel-magic?p=1016017#post1016017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You can solve Demesne problem with Temporal Unstable Condition - once your own Pattern is creating Paradox, even Demesne will not save you.</div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't actually solve the problem because you don't acquire that Condition you made up until after you use the Demesne to travel back in time as far as you want (Verge symbolism willing). Nah, the book's solution seems to work better simply by limiting the availability of places you can use the Verge trick. Although, a Mage could intentionally create a properly symbolic demesne pretty easily, but that kind of hubris is to be encouraged really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}